# Word Battler — Project Rules

We are building an educational vocabulary pet battler. Combat is turn-based and driven by word combinations, grammar, and morphology — not generic RPG stats alone. Prefer designs that teach vocabulary while remaining fun to play.

## Stack

- Web-first: Phaser.js for combat/scenes, React for UI/shell, Tailwind CSS for styling.
- TypeScript throughout. Keep modules small and responsibilities clear.
- Prefer JSON schemas for creatures, moves, vocabulary entries, and combat effects.

## Combat & Pedagogy

- Attacks, synergies, and outcomes should map to language knowledge: definitions, word relationships, and sentence construction.
- Morphology (roots, affixes, compounds) and grammar (e.g. adjective + noun) should produce meaningful combat effects.
- Do not reduce combat to unrelated numbers that ignore the linguistic system.

## Architecture

- Layer 1 — Word Knowledge: definitions and contextual recognition.
- Layer 2 — Word Relationships: affixes, roots, compound words.
- Layer 3 — Sentence Construction: grammar synergies (e.g. adjective + noun).

Keep these layers explicit in data and code. New features should fit a layer rather than invent a parallel combat system.

## Conventions

- Write clean, modular TypeScript.
- Maintain clear JSON schemas for creatures and vocabulary.
- Keep educational intent visible in naming, data, and UI copy.
- Prefer reusable language-system primitives over one-off move hardcoding.
